 with billing access. Asaas credentials and webhook secrets stay in server-side
 configuration and are never exposed to clients.
 
+### Tenant context
+
+Every request that works inside an entity goes through the `current_entity`
+middleware. It reads the session entity (`App\Tenancy\CurrentEntity`) and
+refuses a session entity the user does not belong to with 403. It then binds a
+per-request `App\Tenancy\TenantContext` (entity and membership). Only the HTTP
+layer reads the session key; domain code and Livewire components take the
+entity from the route or from the tenant context.
+
+Authorization still goes through policies (`app/Policies/`), not the session:
+a valid session for entity A grants nothing on the route for entity B.
+
 ### Observability
 
 Application logs, audit trails and human-pageable Discord alerts are separate
